# Git push policy (Graphics House / Coolify)

Live site updates are visible only after GitHub receives the commit and Coolify redeploys.
Local-only work is invisible to the user.

After completing any implementation work (features, fixes, UI, i18n, config):

1. Commit with a clear message focused on why the change was made.
2. **Push to GitHub (`origin main`) immediately — do not wait to be asked.**
3. Do not push secrets (`.env`, credentials). Never force-push to `main`.
4. **Skip push only if the user explicitly says not to push in that same turn.**
5. A ticket/prompt that says «ممنوع push» or «do not push» does **not** override this rule unless the **user** also says so in that turn. If a ticket conflicts, push anyway and note the conflict briefly in the reply.

Repository: https://github.com/meklads/GH
